      "content": "Firstly, compassion for yourself. Feeling guilty or disappointed in your past inaction is a common response, but it's important to acknowledge that a single act or lack of it defines our entire character, which isn't true. By witnessing bullying, you still undoubtedly have qualities of empathy and kindness. Everyone makes mistakes and has the opportunity to learn and grow from their experiences.\n\nTake some time for self-reflection and possibly seek therapy where you can safely explore these feelings. It can also be helpful to engage in small, everyday acts of kindness or to stand up against bullying in ways that feel comfortable to you. Remember, everyone holds immense potential and positive aspects in themselves. You're not a hollow person; you just need time to heal and recognize hidden strengths within yourself.",
